00:18:47,620 --> 00:18:50,037
I guess things are starting
to heat up down there.

267
00:18:50,120 --> 00:18:51,885
I hope they don't need a hand.

268
00:18:53,460 --> 00:18:54,477
Well, whatever.

269
00:18:54,560 --> 00:18:56,697
I gotta find that rock guy.

270
00:18:56,780 --> 00:18:58,220
What a pain.

271
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:04,617
Well, I suppose I shouldn't
delay this further.

272
00:19:04,700 --> 00:19:06,320
Shut your damn mouth!

273
00:19:09,700 --> 00:19:12,700
How can you still be alive, Doflamingo?

274
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:21,560
Do you want me to show you how to
properly behead a man? Soldier!

275
00:19:22,020 --> 00:19:23,079
Kidos, behind you!

276
00:19:25,720 --> 00:19:26,840
Just like this.

277
00:19:29,720 --> 00:19:30,550
Kidos, no!

278
00:19:37,720 --> 00:19:39,000
Damn Straw Hat!

279
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:46,249
There's two young masters?

280
00:19:50,600 --> 00:19:52,500
Sorry, by mistake.

281
00:19:52,760 --> 00:19:55,480
Hey, jerk, gump, gump!

282
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:57,820
Huh, armaments.

283
00:20:01,920 --> 00:20:02,960
Jack Statlin!

284
00:20:15,220 --> 00:20:16,050
Huh?

285
00:20:35,580 --> 00:20:36,840
Lufin-Lan!

286
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:39,760
But how?

287
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:41,220
He has a double?

288
00:20:43,760 --> 00:20:44,780
That hurt.

289
00:20:47,620 --> 00:20:50,820
It seems he's made a
marionette out of his strength.

290
00:20:51,180 --> 00:20:53,120
That technique, what is it?

291
00:20:54,940 --> 00:20:58,500
Rick, a quick question.

292
00:20:59,080 --> 00:21:02,940
Do you remember how you felt
that evening ten years ago?

293
00:21:04,260 --> 00:21:10,260
The one where you torched the town and
sliced your beloved citizens to pieces?

294
00:21:13,760 --> 00:21:15,180
Please, kill me!

295
00:21:17,960 --> 00:21:20,420
I could never forget such a tragedy.

296
00:21:21,060 --> 00:21:23,500
That nightmare haunts me to this day.

297
00:21:24,280 --> 00:21:28,940
Compared to what's about to unfold,
that will seem like a sweet memory.

298
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:30,390
Hmm?

299
00:21:34,360 --> 00:21:36,420
You're mad. What are you planning?

300
00:21:36,620 --> 00:21:38,677
You cannot repeat such a callous act.

301
00:21:38,760 --> 00:21:39,590
Hush now.

302
00:21:39,673 --> 00:21:42,620
I'm going to release you all pika I

303
00:21:46,900 --> 00:21:49,800
Think it's time you scatter these roaches

304
00:22:15,720 --> 00:22:21,300
The Flamingo, you have done
enough damage to these people!

305
00:22:31,320 --> 00:22:33,460
Don't put them through anymore!

306
00:22:34,380 --> 00:22:36,200
Hang on, guys!

307
00:22:36,660 --> 00:22:37,880
Gum-Gum!

308
00:22:39,600 --> 00:22:40,720
Nooo! No!

309
00:23:07,040 --> 00:23:09,275
He chucked us right out of the palace.

310
00:23:10,540 --> 00:23:14,540
There's no chance of us getting
near Doflamingo if Pika is with him.

311
00:23:16,840 --> 00:23:17,840
A birdcage.

312
00:23:19,760 --> 00:23:20,590
It's starting.

313
00:23:40,540 --> 00:23:41,370
Skye!

314
00:23:41,453 --> 00:23:42,283
What's that, sir?

315
00:23:44,600 --> 00:23:45,620
Who knows?

316
00:23:45,800 --> 00:23:47,447
Let's not stay and find out!

317
00:23:48,480 --> 00:23:52,774
We're no match for Doflamingo, so
there's no point in lashing out at him!

318
00:23:52,980 --> 00:23:55,540
Captain, watch out! Something's there!

319
00:23:58,560 --> 00:23:59,390
Why?

320
00:24:00,580 --> 00:24:01,800
Huh? Razors?

321
00:24:02,680 --> 00:24:03,510
Huh?

322
00:24:03,593 --> 00:24:04,608
Are these bars always here?

323
00:24:06,900 --> 00:24:11,660
Before the truth behind this regime
even has a chance to get out.

324
00:24:13,560 --> 00:24:17,140
Doflamingo will kill
every person in Dressrosa.

325
00:24:20,480 --> 00:24:23,220
This fence stretches as far as we can see.

326
00:24:24,820 --> 00:24:26,180
What the hell?

327
00:24:26,380 --> 00:24:27,680
Where's the exit?

328
00:24:35,880 --> 00:24:38,257
What are these beams around us?

329
00:24:38,340 --> 00:24:41,760
Vice Admiral Bastille, I
can't contact headquarters.

330
00:24:42,320 --> 00:24:44,000
What? Same here.

331
00:24:44,320 --> 00:24:46,857
I'm having technical
difficulties reaching the base.

332
00:24:46,940 --> 00:24:49,705
How am I going to report
the events from today?

333
00:24:59,680 --> 00:25:00,510
Hey!

334
00:25:00,593 --> 00:25:02,260
Don't fire at someone's home!

335
00:25:02,960 --> 00:25:03,790
I...

336
00:25:03,873 --> 00:25:04,703
I didn't...

337
00:25:04,786 --> 00:25:07,440
I can't control my own body!

338
00:25:08,340 --> 00:25:09,700
Hey! Stop that!

339
00:25:14,940 --> 00:25:17,360
My arm's moving on its own!

340
00:25:24,820 --> 00:25:26,577
Stop me!

341
00:25:26,660 --> 00:25:28,360
Everybody, stop!

342
00:25:34,120 --> 00:25:35,620
Parasite String

343
00:25:37,720 --> 00:25:39,240
Sir, reporting in.

344
00:25:39,540 --> 00:25:42,180
It's pandemonium all across Dressrosa.

345
00:25:42,580 --> 00:25:45,404
Everyone's going wild and
attacking one another.

346
00:25:48,580 --> 00:25:52,992
I'm sad to inform you that there's even
submarines attacking the civilians.

347
00:25:53,160 --> 00:25:56,180
We need backup or many
innocent people will die.

348
00:25:58,140 --> 00:25:59,680
What's going on now?

349
00:26:04,740 --> 00:26:07,800
The King's Plateau is sinking!

350
00:26:12,260 --> 00:26:13,100
Hey!

351
00:26:13,520 --> 00:26:15,160
Why is the ground shaky?

352
00:26:15,540 --> 00:26:16,720
Who's doing this?

353
00:26:17,120 --> 00:26:18,060
It's Pika.

354
00:26:21,220 --> 00:26:24,044
He's changing the terrain
with his stone powers.

355
00:26:26,040 --> 00:26:28,640
The royal palace is running away!

356
00:26:29,700 --> 00:26:30,530
Stop!

357
00:26:30,840 --> 00:26:32,360
You get back here!

358
00:26:41,900 --> 00:26:43,080
Look out!

359
00:26:43,300 --> 00:26:45,440
The factory is ascending! What?

360
00:26:45,640 --> 00:26:47,169
How is that even possible?

361
00:26:50,280 --> 00:26:51,300
Help me!

362
00:26:53,800 --> 00:26:56,240
Please stop me!

363
00:27:00,660 --> 00:27:02,520
Look at the flower field!

364
00:27:03,180 --> 00:27:04,860
It's rising up!

365
00:27:05,060 --> 00:27:07,760
And pulling the whole town with it!

366
00:27:24,900 --> 00:27:28,417
Citizens and guests of
Dressrosa, greetings.

367
00:27:28,500 --> 00:27:30,180
Might I have a word?

368
00:27:31,480 --> 00:27:36,120
When I started my reign, I could have
easily ruled over you with an iron fist.

369
00:27:36,720 --> 00:27:38,480
Instead, I was benevolent.

370
00:27:39,500 --> 00:27:41,400
But now that you know the truth,

371
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:47,120
there's no doubt in my mind that the vast
majority of you would like to see me dead.

372
00:27:48,180 --> 00:27:51,120
That's why I've prepared
a little game for you.

373
00:27:54,480 --> 00:27:57,700
Your objective is to assassinate me.

374
00:27:58,500 --> 00:28:00,940
You can find me in the royal palace.

375
00:28:01,220 --> 00:28:03,060
I won't be going anywhere.

376
00:28:03,640 --> 00:28:05,740
Take my life and the game ends.

377
00:28:06,520 --> 00:28:08,160
I die, you win.

378
00:28:08,500 --> 00:28:09,700
Real simple, right?

379
00:28:11,420 --> 00:28:15,560
And since I'm so generous, I'll give
you a second way to win as well.

380
00:28:16,480 --> 00:28:20,460
I'm about to read out a list of
people, so get your pencils ready.

381
00:28:21,020 --> 00:28:24,580
Should you manage to bring me
their dead bodies, you win.

382
00:28:25,120 --> 00:28:30,120
Also, I will award a sizable bounty
for each and every head I receive.

383
00:28:32,200 --> 00:28:34,660
It's kill or be killed.

384
00:28:39,980 --> 00:28:43,460
Every person in the kingdom
is now a bounty hunter.

385
00:28:43,900 --> 00:28:46,240
And the only way for you to survive

386
00:28:47,200 --> 00:28:50,300
is for you to take the
life of another person.
